## Flags for the node behind `flzvm rpc` and `flzvm remote`, which is the node
## every `flz` verb starts. Customize: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here
##
## This node connects to the controller, evaluates there and exits. It does no
## dispatch of its own, so it is sized for one call rather than for the host.
## The controller's own flags are in vm.args, a separate file the launcher reads
## for the start commands only.

## One scheduler, and no dirty IO pool. The work is on the other node.
+S 1:1
+SDio 1

## The same ceiling the controller pins, for the same reason. This node opens
## two ports and was allocating a table for a million of them: 15 MB of RSS on
## every verb.
+Q 65536

## The break handler off: SIGINT ends this node instead of opening the BREAK
## menu, so Ctrl-C ends a verb that streams and the controller sees its caller go.
+Bd

## Reclaiming refc binaries more aggressively is a memory-drift remedy, chosen
## against a measured series rather than set here. See
## docs/operations/memory_drift.md.

## Enable deployment without epmd
## (requires changing both vm.args and remote.vm.args)
##-start_epmd false -erl_epmd_port 6789 -dist_listen false
